{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNzQx","is_bot":false,"login":"Soph","name":"Stefan Haubold"},"body":"Investigated a bit why my commits suddenly today were super slow and turns out we have a logic that waits for Claude to finish writing logs. The timeout is 3s and was looking for newer messages. If you did a commit with some delay after the prompt finished you would always wait 3s per session.
This was build when the only place we looked at logs was the stop hook being called and there could be some delay. The same method is now called in multiple places and especially in the pre and post commit hooks. That means the code was waiting while the logs were for sure already done.

There is maybe room for more improvements here, and theoretically a commit while a claude session is still running could still be slow, but that is already a bit messy to do that.","files":[{"path":"cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go","additions":14,"deletions":6},{"path":"cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go","additions":26,"deletions":19},{"path":"cmd/entire/cli/strategy/phase_postcommit_test.go","additions":115,"deletions":0}],"labels":[],"title":"Commit hanging while waiting for transcript update that will never come"}

